The input port Pose accepts a three-element state vector of xy-positions and vehicle heading, [x y theta]. The input port Waypoints accepts an N-by-2 matrix as xy-coordinates. The output ports Linear Velocity and Angular Velocity return linear and angular velocities as scalar values, respectively. The Target Direction port outputs an angle with respect to the forward direction of the robot with positive angles measured counter-clockwise. 

Set the Lookahead distance to tune how closely the robot follows the path. A smaller Lookahead distance improves path tracking but can lead to instability.</block_desc><block_path>$bdroot/Pure Pursuit</block_path><block_open>$bdroot/Pure Pursuit</block_open><block_isNotLeafBlk>0</block_isNotLeafBlk><block_position>720  100  870  180</block_position><block_icon>Pure@20@Pursuit.svg</block_icon><keywords></keywords><port_domains>signal.in_signal:2,signal.out_signal:2</port_domains><block_type>MATLABSystem</block_type><block_reference>robotalgslib/Pure Pursuit</block_reference></block_node></library>